---

<Layout
  title={`${vesselName} Yacht Charter Phuket | 90ft Classic Motor Yacht`}
  description="Private yacht charter in Phuket on Maha Bhetra, a 90ft wooden motor yacht designed by Amanpuri architect Ed Tuttle. Day trips for 12, overnight for 6, Phang Nga Bay & Similans."
  image="/images/yacht/maha-bhetra/maha-bhetra-luxury-yacht-phang-nga-bay-side-view.webp"
>
  <main class="pcom-wrapper">
    
    <section class="pcom-hero">
      <span class="pcom-subtitle">90ft Thai-Crafted Motor Yacht</span>
      <h1 class="pcom-title">{vesselName} Yacht Charter Phuket</h1>
      <div class="pcom-divider"></div>
      <p class="pcom-tagline">{tagline}</p>
    </section>

    <section class="pcom-specs-container">
      <div class="pcom-specs-grid">
        {technicalSpecs.map((spec) => (
          <div class="spec-item">
            <span class="spec-label">{spec.label}</span>
            <span class="spec-value">{spec.value}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pcom-gallery-section">
      <div class="gallery-slider-outer">
        <div id="slider" class="gallery-slider-inner no-scrollbar">
          {slideshow.map((slide, index) => (
            <div class="gallery-slide">
              <OptimizedImage 
                src={slide.img} 
                alt={slide.text}
                loading="lazy"
                widths={[480, 800, 1200]}
                sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px"
              />
              <div class="gallery-caption">
                <span class="caption-count">Vessel Tour {index + 1} / {slideshow.length}</span>
                <p class="caption-text">{slide.text}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <button id="prevBtn" class="nav-button prev" aria-label="Previous">
          <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15.75 19.5L8.25 12l7.5-7.5"></path></svg>
        </button>
        <button id="nextBtn" class="nav-button next" aria-label="Next">
          <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M8.25 4.5l7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5"></path></svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pcom-content-grid">
      <div class="content-main">
        <h2 class="content-heading">Private Yacht Charter in Phuket aboard Maha Bhetra</h2>
        <div class="heading-line"></div>
        <p class="paragraph">
          <strong>Maha Bhetra</strong> is a <strong>90ft (27.4 m) classic motor yacht</strong>, built by hand in Thailand with a timber hull and designed by <strong>Ed Tuttle</strong>, the architect behind Amanpuri and the Aman resorts. She is available for <strong>private day charters for up to 12 guests</strong> and <strong>overnight charters for up to 6 guests</strong>, departing from Phuket Yacht Haven Marina towards Phang Nga Bay, Krabi, Koh Phi Phi and the Similan Islands.
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Tuttle drew only one yacht in his career and kept her for himself until his death in 2020. For thirty years she has stayed with the same family, cared for rather than rebuilt: the Jim Thompson silks he chose, the eighteenth-century Southeast Asian antiques in the saloon and the teak joinery are all original. This is a genuine classic yacht, not a modern copy of one.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">Designed by Ed Tuttle, the Architect of Amanpuri</h3>
        <p class="paragraph">
          American architect and interior designer Edward Burnham Tuttle Jr. (1945 to 2020) studied at the University of Washington, was influenced by Frank Lloyd Wright and Mies van der Rohe, and opened his studio, Design Realization, in Paris in 1977. Over four decades he shaped the look of the Aman group, from Amanpuri in Phuket to Amanjena in Morocco, proving that restraint can be the purest form of luxury.
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Maha Bhetra follows the same ideas as his resorts: Thai craftsmanship and local materials, spaces that open to the sea breeze and almost no decoration that does not have a purpose. The louvred cabinets, the proportions of the saloon and the stepped ceiling above the dining table are his design, and the exclusive Jim Thompson fabric he commissioned for her cushions is still aboard.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">A Thai Timber Hull Built for the Andaman Sea</h3>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Her lines come from traditional Thai working boats: a long, slim wooden hull with a fine bow and a draft of 2.5 metres, shallow enough to anchor close to the beach. Guests sleep below and live on the upper deck, the opposite of most modern charter yachts, which is why Maha Bhetra feels more like a floating house than a boat.
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          As a displacement yacht she cruises at a steady 8 knots, uses little fuel and runs quietly enough to talk on the aft deck while under way. She is made for slow, relaxed island hopping in the Andaman Sea rather than rushing between crowded beaches.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">Open-Plan Teak Saloon and Bow Daybed</h3>
        <p class="paragraph">
          The entire upper deck is living space. Teak floors, a teak ceiling and sliding louvred panels turn the saloon and the aft deck into a single room that opens on three sides to the sea and the view. A round table seats all six overnight guests for dinner and a wide banquette wraps around the stern.
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          At the bow, a teak daybed for four sits under full-day shade, and in the evening the crew sets dinner on the foredeck facing the limestone karsts of Phang Nga Bay.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">Three Identical 20 sqm Double Cabins</h3>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Below deck there is no master cabin and no small cabin. All three double cabins measure 20 sqm, with two 140 x 200 cm berths, air conditioning, a vanity, two wardrobes in a dressing area and an en-suite bathroom with separate shower and WC. Every guest gets the same comfort, so choosing cabins is simply a matter of preference.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">Thai Cuisine and Full Board</h3>
        <p class="paragraph">
          The cook buys fresh from the local market each morning. Thai cuisine is the crew's speciality and the dish most guests ask for again, but a continental breakfast or a seafood barbecue on the beach are just as easy. Overnight charters are full board, including snacks, fruit, drinking water, tea, coffee, soft drinks, local beer and one bottle of French rosé per day.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">An Experienced Thai Crew</h3>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Maha Bhetra sails with a crew of five, and the three senior members have spent more than seventy years aboard between them. They know every quiet anchorage, which bays stay calm in a northerly wind and the best fishing spots along the coast. All three love fishing, and most guests end up joining them.
        </p>
        <ul class="toy-list">
          {crew.map(member => <li><strong>{member.name}</strong>, {member.role}. {member.note}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="paragraph" style="font-size: 13px; color: #4f5059;">Crew composition may change; the current crew list is confirmed before departure.</p>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">Kayaks, Paddleboard and Snorkelling Included</h3>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Thanks to her 2.5 m draft, Maha Bhetra anchors close to shore. The tender takes you onto beaches that day-trip boats cannot reach, and the kayaks explore further into mangroves and the hidden lagoons (hongs) of Phang Nga Bay. All water toys are on board and included, with no need to book in advance.
        </p>
        <ul class="toy-list">
          {waterToys.map(toy => <li>{toy}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <h3 class="sub-heading">On Board</h3>
        <ul class="toy-list">
          {onBoard.map(item => <li>{item}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="content-sidebar">
        <div class="booking-sticky-box">
          <h3 class="sidebar-heading">Ready to Charter?</h3>
          <p class="sidebar-text">Check availability for a private day or overnight charter on the 90ft classic motor yacht Maha Bhetra, departing from Phuket Yacht Haven Marina.</p>
          <a href="https://wa.me/66918233120?text=Hi%20Luna%20Diving!%20I'm%20interested%20in%20booking%20Maha%20Bhetra." target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="pcom-btn-primary">
            Inquire via WhatsApp
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Day Charter Pricing Section -->
    <section class="pcom-pricing-section">
      <div class="pricing-header">
        <h2 class="content-heading">Day Charter Rates</h2>
        <p class="paragraph" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">One day, up to twelve guests (Per Charter, Thai Baht & US Dollar)</p>
        <div class="heading-line"></div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="pcom-cabins-list">
        {dayCharterRates.map((rate) => (
          <div class="cabin-rate-card">
            <div class="cabin-main-info">
              <h3 class="cabin-name">{rate.name}</h3>
              <span class="cabin-location">Itineraries: Kai & Naka, Phang Nga Bay, Koh Maiton, Koh Hong</span>
              <p class="cabin-details">{rate.details}</p>
              <span class="cabin-trip-tag">Day Trip</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cabin-price-zone" style="text-align: right;">
              <div style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
                <span style="font-size: 10px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #4f5059; display: block;">All Year</span>
                <span class="price-amount" style="font-size: 16px;">{rate.allYearTHB}</span>
                <span class="price-label">{rate.allYearUSD}</span>
              </div>
              <div style="border-top: 1px solid #f1f1f4; padding-top: 6px;">
                <span style="font-size: 10px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #4f5059; display: block;">Peak Season (20 Dec - 10 Jan)</span>
                <span class="price-amount" style="font-size: 16px;">{rate.peakTHB}</span>
                <span class="price-label">{rate.peakUSD}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Overnight Charter Rates Table -->
    <section class="pcom-schedule-section">
      <div class="pricing-header">
        <h2 class="content-heading">Overnight Charter Rates</h2>
        <p class="paragraph" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Up to six guests (Per Charter, Thai Baht & US Dollar)</p>
        <div class="heading-line"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="table-responsive-container">
        <table class="schedule-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Duration</th>
              <th>All Year</th>
              <th>Peak Season (20 Dec - 10 Jan)</th>
              <th>Similan Islands (4+ Days)</th>
              <th class="table-action-header">Action</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {overnightRates.map((row) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="td-dates">{row.duration}</td>
                <td class="td-itinerary">
                  <div><strong>{row.allYearTHB}</strong></div>
                  <div class="price-sub-usd">{row.allYearUSD}</div>
                </td>
                <td class="td-itinerary">
                  <div><strong>{row.peakTHB}</strong></div>
                  <div class="price-sub-usd">{row.peakUSD}</div>
                </td>
                <td class="td-itinerary">
                  <div><strong>{row.similanTHB}</strong></div>
                  <div class="price-sub-usd">{row.similanUSD}</div>
                </td>
                <td class="td-action">
                  <a href={`https://wa.me/66918233120?text=Hi%20Luna%20Diving!%20I'm%20interested%20in%20booking%20Maha%20Bhetra%20(${encodeURIComponent(row.duration)}).`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="table-book-btn">
                    Book
                  </a>
                </td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="table-note-text" style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 12px; color: #4f5059; line-height: 1.5;">
        * Rates are set in Thai Baht, include local VAT, and are per charter, not per person.<br/>
        * Peak season is 20 December to 10 January.<br/>
        * The Similan Islands can be reached on charters of four days or more, at the rate in the third column; Similan national park fees are not included.<br/>
        * US dollar figures are shown for guidance only, converted at THB 33 to USD 1.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="pcom-details-grid-section">
      <div class="details-split-container">
        <div class="details-column included-box">
          <h3 class="details-col-title">
            <svg class="title-icon icon-inc" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path>
            </svg>
            What's Included
          </h3>
          <ul class="details-list">
            {includedItems.map((item) => (
              <li class="details-item">
                <svg class="item-dot dot-inc" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 8 8"><circle cx="4" cy="4" r="3"/></svg>
                <span>{item}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="details-column excluded-box">
          <h3 class="details-col-title">
            <svg class="title-icon icon-exc" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9.75 9.75l4.5 4.5m0-4.5l-4.5 4.5M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path>
            </svg>
            Not Included & Conditions
          </h3>
          <ul class="details-list">
            {notIncludedItems.map((item) => (
              <li class="details-item exc-item">
                <svg class="item-dot dot-exc" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 8 8"><circle cx="4" cy="4" r="3"/></svg>
                <div class="exc-text-wrapper">
                  <span class="exc-main-text">{item.text}</span>
                  {item.highlight && <span class="exc-highlight">{item.highlight}</span>}
                </div>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
